{"ts":"2026-08-13T21:25:10.666Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"b655077c4be079601c2b813e","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.231","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-kyjdne"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"The degradation ladder only sees top-level arrays, so the governance reads whose bulk is nested skip every intermediate rung and return nothing at all"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"compactRowsToBudget reduces the largest row collection until the estimate fits the ceiling. readOutputRowPaths resolves which collections those are: a declared row_contract when present, and otherwise the top-level array properties of the result. Governance reads do not put their bulk at the top level, so for those commands the ladder has almost nothing to reduce and falls straight through to the last rung, which omits the entire result.\n\nMeasured 2026-08-13 at HEAD build 2026.8.13, on the exact invocation AGENTS.md prescribes for diagnostics:\n\n  pm validate --check-resolution --check-history-drift --json\n\nUnbounded, this is 81,108 bytes, about 20,277 estimated tokens against a governance JSON ceiling of 9,000. Its array collections are:\n\n  295   checks.0.details.missing_resolution_rows\n  295   checks.0.details.missing_resolution_remediation_hints\n    2   checks\n    1   warnings\n\nBoth 295-row collections are two levels below the root, so neither is visible to row discovery. The only reducible collection is checks, which halves from 2 to 1 and then falls under the length > 1 guard. The one surviving check still carries both 295-row arrays, the estimate is still far above the ceiling, and the result is discarded whole.\n\nWhat the caller receives is two keys: output_budget_exceeded and read_output. So the diagnostic the project routes its own agents to returns no verdict, no ok field, and no findings in JSON at the default budget. The result is recoverable with --output-budget unbounded, which the envelope does name, so this is a recovery cost rather than a dead end; but the recovery is the whole 20,277 tokens, because the intermediate rungs that exist to avoid exactly that were unreachable.\n\nThe receipt cannot explain its own decision. omitReadOutputForBudget builds a minimal receipt and then estimates it, so the emitted values are estimated_tokens 125, budget_tokens 9000, result_omitted true. The number reported is the size of the refusal, not the size of what was refused, and read as written the receipt says a 125-token result was dropped for exceeding a 9,000-token ceiling.\n\nThis is the mechanism behind pm-5t33or's second and fifth criteria rather than a restatement of them: the ladder is declared and implemented, and it is inapplicable to the shape most governance output actually has. It is also why the shape question is not cosmetic — a nested payload is not merely more expensive to read, it is unreachable by every bound the contract provides except the one that returns nothing."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","area:sdk","contracts","governance","output-contract","token-efficiency"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-13T21:25:10.666Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-13T21:25:10.666Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":240},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Row-collection discovery reaches nested collections, so a command whose payload sits below the top level is reducible by the same ladder as one whose payload sits at it; The whole-result omission rung is reachable only after every earlier rung has been applied and has failed to fit, proven by a case whose bulk is nested; The omission receipt reports the estimated size of the result that was omitted, not the size of the envelope that reports the omission; The AGENTS.md-prescribed diagnostic invocation returns a machine-readable verdict at the default budget, or the recommendation names the budget it needs; A regression test drives a real nested-payload governance read past its ceiling and asserts the rung that fired"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-33cw"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"036a35f08ddca50ec62a565393112042a2de6433d65b46844520dbe87f9b2ef3","item_hash_version":2,"message":""}
